the sovereign; we can say *His access to fortune was barred,* or *His accession to fortune had not yet taken place,* but not the converse. The idea of increase, often present in *accession,* is foreign to *access*; *an access of fury, fever, joy, despair, &c.,* is a fit or sudden attack of it, which may occur whatever the previous
